                <pb facs="0359" n="241" sameAs="frus:frus1928v02/pg241"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.00/10077: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in China</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >MacMurray</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Extract]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Peking</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1928-06-12T20:00:00+08:00"><hi rendition="#italic">June 12, 1928—8
                                p.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received June 13—9:55
                    a.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>458. My No. 404 [<hi rendition="#italic">444</hi>], June 10, 1 a.m. [<hi
                        rendition="#italic">p.m.</hi>] General Yen Hsi-shan arrived here yesterday
                    and took up his headquarters at the Ministry of War as garrison commander of the
                    Peking-Tientsin area. Proclamation issued by Yen states that he assumes full
                    responsibility for the maintenance of law and order, and for the protection of
                    both Chinese and foreign lives and property. …</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">MacMurray</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
